§§ lhde is meant as a serious Unix desktop environment, not a Linux-only curiosity.  It builds and runs on FreeBSD 15 with the same tests, the hardware controls have a back end per system behind one interface, scripts avoid /proc and GNU-only tools, and portability is one compatibility header, not ifdefs.

§§ Wayland is a different story and a later one; the X-specific code is confined to a few files, which keeps it possible.  Fedora on the second laptop is where that experiment would start.
